{"event_type":"review","id":"95c6f6ea3c57cd43a88cab203fbf981c28cbc2e5eafe0780418f3e4ee3ab4a35","occurred_at":"2026-11-08T15:07:53Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/9e5bb788812b79e028723ca162645430b4cd416416c61594a568366d4123a1ea","sha256":"9e5bb788812b79e028723ca162645430b4cd416416c61594a568366d4123a1ea"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/3751c9fc58e0d49a24cfe5c7c10d76035dbb8aab6967da6a73737ac42e82ea6a","sha256":"3751c9fc58e0d49a24cfe5c7c10d76035dbb8aab6967da6a73737ac42e82ea6a"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/e08b3d1617954ede2ce691ba903e73efcd5b5d94b64ebaded7a821e9b216cfb3","sha256":"e08b3d1617954ede2ce691ba903e73efcd5b5d94b64ebaded7a821e9b216cfb3"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/4cab290299e687972fcdc5e305c624655699d0049526092ae952c1b3fcd4494f","sha256":"4cab290299e687972fcdc5e305c624655699d0049526092ae952c1b3fcd4494f"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/5a7bf7b00e3e94daaacf2d7757f41f5964e70247b364bddcf1b53bd9e12b6c7b","sha256":"5a7bf7b00e3e94daaacf2d7757f41f5964e70247b364bddcf1b53bd9e12b6c7b"}],"attempt_id":"6ae79b921229b27a2a2faba33d189d297c4409cd8a27e8dc25e94d0188cc2578:0:1","base":"1b8db38a95adb8d1fac88ad01439e5c527d9b03d","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"9c66f1625f68318f19e03591528ba7cc6be24029","body":"**Lost-acknowledgement reconciliation fails for uppercase SHAs.**\n\nLine 38 accepts uppercase hex because of the `/i` flag. `git ls-remote` prints lowercase object names. If the caller passes an uppercase `sha`, the comparison on Line 61 never matches. Git accepts the uppercase SHA in the push, so the push can succeed on the remote while the acknowledgement is lost. The function then returns the failed `result` instead of the success result. The caller sees a failure for a publication that happened, which is a false negative.\n\nLowercase `sha` in the comparison. Alternatively, remove the `i` flag on Line 38 so the function rejects non-canonical SHAs up front.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-    if (remote.code === 0 && remote.stdout.trim() === `${sha}\\t${ref}`)\n+    if (remote.code === 0 && remote.stdout.trim() === `${sha.toLowerCase()}\\t${ref}`)\n```\n</details>\n\n\n\n\n\nAlso applies to: 61-62","id":"7242c37e58716cd06646701c7e79fd49686fb56562282c270a519b9684023e6e","intervals":[],"path":"src/adapters/git/leasedPush.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Lost-acknowledgement reconciliation fails for uppercase SHAs."}],"head":"f622f2e7d0132e2a05b5d2822b953e919f3423e3","head_tree":"f3d13794b479ccd72ccb765c7289aa9698c4c59f","input_scope":[{"blob":"9c66f1625f68318f19e03591528ba7cc6be24029","intervals":[[1,67]],"path":"src/adapters/git/leasedPush.ts"}],"job_id":"6ae79b921229b27a2a2faba33d189d297c4409cd8a27e8dc25e94d0188cc2578:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"9c66f1625f68318f19e03591528ba7cc6be24029","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/adapters/git/leasedPush.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"}],"policy_digest":"eacd1bcf42a0e72eca72fcf9c1e9c8f97e7c515cd67a8fa7965c966924647693","repo":"camerontaylor/cq-toolkit","requested_scope":[{"blob":"9c66f1625f68318f19e03591528ba7cc6be24029","intervals":[[1,67]],"path":"src/adapters/git/leasedPush.ts"}],"reviewed_scope":[{"blob":"9c66f1625f68318f19e03591528ba7cc6be24029","intervals":[[1,67]],"path":"src/adapters/git/leasedPush.ts"}],"scope_digest":"670e4fd0744d57b8b7a201e7d01500af62af0bb2e5f98917573007259104bdf6","source":{"authenticated":true,"id":"backfill-6ae79b921229b27a2a2faba33d189d297c4409cd8a27e8dc25e94d0188cc2578-g0-20261108T150620Z","producer":"crq-runner-app","repo":"camerontaylor/cq-toolkit",